        "note": "Palomar entry PALOMAR-2026-10-23-000009 (version 1): the O(n log n) bound of the same repository (Casteigts–Peters–Schoeters 2019 via SAND 2025; github.com/dracoanguis/temporal-graphs, branch nlogn-spanner-dismountability-submission, commit 79214ea). The statement of record uses verbatim the same definitions (IsLocallyInjective, Journey, IsTemporalSpanner, namespace TemporalCliqueSpanners), and the Solution reuses its bridge to the library unchanged. Both proofs share the dismountability reduction and a generic induction on cliques (exists_isSpannerOf_ncard_le_of_forall_not_twoHopDismountable); only the non-dismountable case differs: one-sided dismountability for O(n log n), extremally matched bi-cliques and stars for 7n.",
